// The prelude floor's own fixture: a program that asks the medium for
// nothing. Whatever `mentl mn-bare-floor.mn cost` reports is the
// vocabulary the medium processes before it can compile a constant —
// 6307 source lines at the pin that measured it, for a program of one.
//
// It exists to be RATCHETED, not to be run. The frontier's cost leg holds
// the line count under a ceiling that may only fall, and what lowers it is
// Hβ.driver.link-is-reachability: judging the prelude decls a program
// actually demands instead of all of them. A rise means the medium began
// processing more source to answer the same trivial question.
//
// Keep it importless and one declaration deep. Any import here would
// measure that import instead of the floor.
fn main() = 7
